Saved 6000 chars from https://hirion.ch/signup -> .agent-log/dom-snippet.html
I fixed the locator that was making `RegistrationTest` fail. The locator-rules check and the test compile both pass, but I haven't re-run the tests against the live site, so whether it actually goes green is still unconfirmed.

**What was failing:** the step 3 role picker locator in `addRole()` (`RegistrationTest.java:246`). The test looked for a combobox named "Add", but the live combobox has no accessible name. That's candidate defect D13 in `docs/intent.md`. So the lookup timed out after 10s. Three tests failed on it: `reg7_stepFourPremiumTrialSelected`, `reg7_freeCanBeSelected` and `reg8_stepsOneToThreeSendNothing`. `reg9`, `reg4` and `auth6` didn't run because they depend on the account-creating `reg9`.

**The change:** it now finds the combobox by its role and its exact visible text "Add":
```java
page.getByRole(AriaRole.COMBOBOX)
      .filter(new Locator.FilterOptions().setHasText(Pattern.compile("^\\s*Add\\s*$"))).click();
```
The comment above `addRole()` now mentions D13. Nothing else changed, and I didn't touch the known-bug test `reg10`.

**Checks:**
- `java scripts/CheckLocatorRules.java src/test/java`: PASS, no forbidden patterns.
- `mvn test-compile`: OK.

**What the fix rests on:** `.agent-log/dom-snippet.html` only contains **step 1** of signup (the capture stops at 6000 bytes), so it doesn't show the step 3 element. I based the fix on the test report's error log and the D13 note from the earlier live run. Keep that in mind when you review it and the heal log before merging.

**Consequence of the workaround:** this locator only works because the site has the D13 bug. If the site later gives the combobox a proper name, the text match should still work. Then it can go back to `role(AriaRole.COMBOBOX, "<name>")`.
